<Base title="About — Shyam Prasad Rao">
  <article class="post">
    <p class="lede">Hi — I'm Shyam.</p>
    <p>I currently lead commercial PC portfolio and technology strategy at HP, working across product architecture, silicon, AI PCs, and critical technologies (e.g., memory, panel, battery) that shape what gets built next.</p>
    <p>My path here has crossed engineering, strategy, and finance. I started as a systems architect building distributed systems, working close to the metal where software, operating systems, and hardware meet. I then spent eight years at Deloitte, advising technology companies on M&amp;A and corporate strategy across software, hardware, and semiconductors. I eventually moved back closer to the technology itself — product portfolio and technology strategy at HP.</p>
    <p>Outside my day job, I spend much of my time exploring quantum computing and AI. I study quantum information and error correction, experiment with ideas at the intersection of machine learning and quantum systems, and build small projects to understand things that interest me. I have also taught portfolio optimization and quantum computing at Chennai Mathematical Institute.</p>
    <p>This site is my working notebook. I write about technology strategy, AI, quantum computing, and anything that piques my interest. Some pieces are polished essays; others are research notes, experiments, or ideas still being worked out.</p>
    <p>You can find my projects on <a href="https://github.com/shyam-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>, or reach me at <a href="mailto:shyamprasadrao@gmail.com">shyamprasadrao@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
